  METHOD GET_COMPLETE_FILE_NAME.
* The objective of the method is to return the complete file name depending on the underlying operating system
    DATA:
      LO_FS_PATH        TYPE REF TO CL_FS_PATH,
      LV_PATH_KIND      TYPE CL_FS_PATH=>PATH_KIND_T,
      LV_FILE_SEPARATOR TYPE C.

    CLEAR RV_COMPLETE_FILE_NAME.

    IF IV_PRESENTATION_SERVER EQ ABAP_TRUE.

      CL_GUI_FRONTEND_SERVICES=>GET_FILE_SEPARATOR( CHANGING FILE_SEPARATOR = LV_FILE_SEPARATOR ).

      IF LV_FILE_SEPARATOR EQ '\'.
        LV_PATH_KIND = CL_FS_PATH=>PATH_KIND_WINDOWS.
      ELSE.
        LV_PATH_KIND = CL_FS_PATH=>PATH_KIND_UNIX.
      ENDIF.

    ELSE.
      LV_PATH_KIND = CL_FS_PATH=>PATH_KIND_SMART.
    ENDIF.

    LO_FS_PATH = CL_FS_PATH=>CREATE( NAME      = IV_FILE_PATH
                                     PATH_KIND = LV_PATH_KIND ).

    LO_FS_PATH->APPEND_PATH_NAME( NAME = IV_FILE_NAME ).
    RV_COMPLETE_FILE_NAME = LO_FS_PATH->GET_PATH_NAME( ).

  ENDMETHOD.